<title>BELGIUM: EU says close to rice import duty deal with U.S..</title>
<headline>EU says close to rice import duty deal with U.S..</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission is close to reaching agreement with the U.S. on the cumulative recovery of rice import duties, an EU official said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The issue is scheduled for discussion and a possible vote on Friday at this week's special two-day cereals management committee meeting.</p>
<p>A U.S. diplomat in Brussels said talks were continuing in a constructive atmosphere.</p>
<p>&quot;There are a number of trade consultations going on and both sides are anxious that they should remain separate from each other. The atmosphere is good,&quot; the diplomat said.</p>
<p>A Commission official said, &quot;We might always get some conclusion.&quot;</p>
<p>The official said the issue also had to be discussed with member states, adding, &quot;It does not only depend on the Americans.&quot;</p>
